; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; What the Huntress moves by -- the Rogue, drawn as neilhancart's "Huntress".
;
; Her skeleton is not the kit's. The Humanoid set's clips are KayKit's and drive
; KayKit bones (hips, upperarm.l); hers is a Maya HumanIK rig
; (QuickRigCharacter_Hips_03 ...), so not one of them would reach her and she
; would stand in her A-pose. So the clips she plays are retargeted onto her own
; bones once, in Blender (art/huntress/export_huntress.py), and written here under
; their libraries' own names:
;
;   KayKit (CC0)     the bow -- Ranged_Bow_Idle, _Aiming_Idle, _Draw, _Release,
;                    _Release_Up -- and Running_A, Death_A, Spawn_Ground
;   Quaternius' UAL  Hit_Chest, Idle_Loop, Death01, Roll, Spell_Simple_Shoot:
;   (CC0)            a grown body's movements, where the chibi's looked wrong on her
;
; Her fingers are keyed into every one of them: the bow hand closed round the
; grip, the other relaxed, or hooked on the string while she shoots.
;
; A clip not listed in CLIPS in her exporter is not here: naming one in rogue.duke
; means adding it there and running ./gradlew exportHuntress.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AnimationSet
  Name = Huntress
  Libraries = [
    animations/characters/huntress.glb,
    ; Her seat on the horse (Ride_Idle, Ride_Gallop): art/mounts/export_riders.py.
    animations/characters/riding_rogue.glb,
  ]
  Idle = Ranged_Bow_Idle
  Walk = Running_A
  Attack = Ranged_Bow_Release
  Death = Death_A
End
